# Solreign "Asset Conduct Charter" — self-antag conduct boundaries, one-page in-game
# readable. Paper content for SolreignSelfAntagConductCharter in
# Resources/Prototypes/_Solreign/Entities/self_antag_conduct_charter.yml.

solreign-conduct-charter-1 =
    SOLREIGN ASSET CONDUCT CHARTER
    RE: Self-Directed Enterprise Initiatives ("Self-Antag")

    Solreign encourages entrepreneurial initiative. Assets who identify
    opportunities for personal enrichment, departmental rivalry, or creative
    asset reallocation are commended — provided the enterprise is
    PROPORTIONATE, ESCALATES WITH VISIBLE BUILD-UP, and remains CONSENSUAL
    in spirit, if not in paperwork.

    APPROVED INITIATIVES:
    - Petty theft, embezzlement, and light fraud (Standing permitting).
    - Office politics: rivalries, sabotage, blackmail, coups.
    - Escalating conflict a reasonable Asset could see coming.
    - Sabotage with a visible build-up. Do not skip to the punchline.

    NOT APPROVED, EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY:
    - Indiscriminate or unprovoked mass casualties. Solreign values its
      headcount, nominally.
    - Targeting newly onboarded Assets. They have not yet signed the
      arbitration clause; you are legally exposed, not just morally.
    - Romantic or sexual roleplay of any kind. Not on Company time, not on
      Company hardware, not ever.
    - Manufacturing incidents solely to inflate your Ledger entry. Auditors
      can tell. Auditors can always tell.

    Violations are reviewed by Human Resources, which is to say: by an
    admin, who is not impressed, and who has a mute button.

    Solreign: Ambition is encouraged. Judgment is mandatory.
